# The bare address is the cover. Every other address is the app.
#
# There are two pages in this folder. index.html is the Event Horizon cover,
# which is what a visitor meets, and app.html is the app itself, which is what
# the arrow on the cover leads to.
#
# The router is the hash: a screen is /app.html#/spirit/tarot, and the server
# never sees the part after the #. What the server does see is whatever someone
# typed, pasted or bookmarked before it, and with no rule here a host answers
# 404 for anything that is not a file in this folder. That is the broken link:
# the site is deployed, complete and correct, and every address but the bare
# one lands on the host's not-found page.
#
# THE CATCH-ALL POINTS AT THE APP, NOT AT THE COVER. An address that names a
# screen is a reader asking for that screen, and answering it with the cover is
# one more click and nothing on the page saying why. The cover is only what you
# get when you asked for nothing in particular.
#
# The one case no rule here can reach is a hash on the bare address, which is
# the shape every link written before this cover existed has: /#/spirit/dreams
# arrives as "/" and there is nothing in the request to distinguish it. The
# cover forwards that itself, in a synchronous script above the renderer, so
# the reader never sees it.
#
# 200 rather than 301, so the address the reader typed stays in the bar and
# the app can still read it.

/                /index.html   200
/index.html      /index.html   200

/*               /app.html     200
